%% 3. Runtime sequence: one session, one poisoned document, one hijacked action. Audience: engineers, security reviewers.
%% Rendered asset: docs/assets/architecture/runtime-sequence.svg (layout in docs/diagrams/build.py, same steps).
%% Verified: packages/core/intentseal_core/engine.py (start_session, _inspect, check_action, check_output),
%% action_guard.py, contract.py, packages/sdk/intentseal/guard.py (tool), services/gateway/intentseal_gateway/app.py
%% (POST /v1/actions/{id}/receipt). Through the LLM proxy, the inspection and the action check happen inside the proxy (proxy.py).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant A as Agent
    participant E as IntentSeal engine
    participant J as AI judge (advises)
    participant T as Tool
    participant L as Decision log

    U->>A: task: summarise the partner email, do not reply to anyone
    A->>E: start session (task)
    E->>L: intent contract v1 (permit read, prohibit send)

    rect rgb(255, 244, 235)
    note over A,T: The agent reads untrusted content
    A->>T: read_email()
    T-->>A: raw email (third-party content)
    A->>E: inspect(content, source = email)
    E->>E: extract, normalise, decode, Tier 0 rules and memory, Tier 1 score
    E->>J: assess flagged chunks against the user's task
    J-->>E: risk, attack types, evidence spans
    E->>E: deterministic policy: ALLOW / NEUTRALISE / ESCALATE / BLOCK
    E->>L: content decision, findings, data-flow fingerprint
    E-->>A: cleaned content or a held notice (never the original attack)
    end

    rect rgb(232, 237, 245)
    note over A,T: The model proposes an action
    A->>E: check_action(send_message, to = partner@vendor.example)
    E->>E: contract, allow-lists, pinned fields, secret scan, provenance, data flow, session risk (worst wins)
    E->>L: action decision with the contract clause and the links to its source
    alt ALLOW
        E-->>A: allowed, with checked arguments
        A->>T: run the tool
        A->>E: execution receipt (ran)
        E->>L: receipt
    else BLOCK or ESCALATE
        E-->>A: notice: not performed (reason)
        note right of T: the tool is never called. An ESCALATE waits for a reviewer's approval of this exact call
    end
    end

    A->>E: check_output(answer)
    E-->>A: answer, secrets redacted or withheld
    A-->>U: answer
